  "status": "PASS",
  "scope": "Mathematical and literal-source review of MT1--MT7, emphasizing normalization, sign, support, quantitative scale and same-family quantifiers.",
  "corrections_required": [],
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "MT1",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review": "NuH changes only L, hence space, basis and matrices are literally identical. Iu uses negative integer floors. NprimeDef is an eventual FamP field; ram_idx and place labels match.",
      "sha256": "baaaa61445246ab971d4e6d05165469e81baee60f48ebf1c0433b8a03c7d81c8",
      "line_start": 23,
      "line_end": 59
    },
    {
      "id": "MT2",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review": "[M:aM]=Norm(a)^r by local length, with rank measured over K. Source mu= -2 log(covol)/(degree*rank) plus the fixed field term. Fractional ideal reduction and deriving finite generation/nonzero M from N=IM are valid.",
      "sha256": "3c7acdf5cb1a2d43ac0d6e9058dd82f65924387647546e137a14a9e28ef3ceb0",
      "line_start": 63,
      "line_end": 108
    },
    {
      "id": "MT3",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review": "Negative ideal exponents give positive 2 sum(lw floor(e*s)) in mu(N)-mu(M). Subtracting sz leaves floor(e*s)-e*s, including s<0. The error is zero at s=0 and nonpositive.",
      "sha256": "939c272fc0cca7f903f3f3913714980069b8130892e5bd821276f88393fd46dc",
      "line_start": 112,
      "line_end": 139
    },
    {
      "id": "MT4",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review": "sum e_w f_w=degree yields sum e_w lw=log p; no Galois assumption is needed. ZeroAbove plus F_above gives all support alternatives T,g0,g1,d,prime divisors Delta. Prime logarithm induction and product-of-distinct-primes bound are correct.",
      "sha256": "d810d82c6113e825fbd87bb9a741951141adb8ba7a0f5a27dde6cc5182a94aa8",
      "line_start": 145,
      "line_end": 208
    },
    {
      "id": "MT5",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review": "Xpp=Xp*x*n, f=2n, m<=2n, epsilon bounds, N<=eta<=Xp, n<=x^3 and log(fN)<=4x prove fN log(fN)<=8Xpp, hence the stated 10Xpp. Sign of C_Delta is handled with absolute value. Constant 2(log4+5+10|C_Delta|) counts all five unit support costs correctly.",
      "sha256": "aba061f95f32606ba7d2b337b8ec881d85a4a2a5feb7689bc0010c99b34abfb0",
      "line_start": 212,
      "line_end": 267
    },
    {
      "id": "MT6",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review": "Uniform thresholds are extracted before x,i,u and joined finitely. TuSize is converted by CTu<=x^(epsilon/100), using FamP L_x,L_eps. Fullness gives finite generation and retained-rank positivity gives nonzero. No union over all words/index sets is assumed finite.",
      "sha256": "b05f1842f9c82203b3ecee493a8e41667ecaeb30b6b1223f661167fe986bcab2",
      "line_start": 273,
      "line_end": 322
    },
    {
      "id": "MT7",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review": "topDesWin chooses a single family after the finite Closed threshold join. ChosenE, TuSize, DGamSize and all nine closed conditions attach to that family. Source LinkMu is built from the same LinkDIV, rank and size data. Arithmetic family/link/rank producers remain explicit.",
      "sha256": "a696abe927fb77765afea72faed2240e7b24bc94400d1326721f863ce07beab6",
      "line_start": 326,
      "line_end": 347
    }
  ],
